      "p0003-n0009-l0001"
    ],
    "source_pages": [
      3
    ],
    "text": "1.1 Non-Technical Explanation"
  },
  {
    "block_id": "b000033",
    "issues": [],
    "kind": "prose",
    "repairs": [
      {
        "left": "p0003-n0010-l0000",
        "operation": "line_wrap_to_space",
        "right": "p0003-n0010-l0001"
      },
      {
        "left": "p0003-n0010-l0001",
        "operation": "line_wrap_to_space",
        "right": "p0003-n0010-l0002"
      },
      {
        "left": "p0003-n0010-l0002",
        "operation": "line_wrap_to_space",
        "right": "p0003-n0010-l0003"
      }
    ],
    "section_id": "s0005",
    "source_line_ids": [
      "p0003-n0010-l0000",
      "p0003-n0010-l0001",
      "p0003-n0010-l0002",
      "p0003-n0010-l0003"
    ],
    "source_pages": [
      3
    ],
    "text": "Why is it so di\ufb03cult to keep the temperature of the water even throughout when taking a bath? In a standard single-faucet bathtub, hot water comes out of the faucet on only one side of the bath, leaving the other side of the bath colder until enough time passes for the temperature to even out. When left running, this might take more time than a user wants to wait for."
  },
  {
    "block_id": "b000034",
    "issues": [],
    "kind": "prose",
    "repairs": [
      {
        "left": "p0003-n0011-l0000",
        "operation": "line_wrap_to_space",
        "right": "p0003-n0011-l0001"
      }
    ],
    "section_id": "s0005",
    "source_line_ids": [
      "p0003-n0011-l0000",
      "p0003-n0011-l0001"
    ],
    "source_pages": [
      3
    ],
    "text": "To further complicate things, hot water is also slightly less dense than cold water, and will thus be more concentrated on the surface of the bathtub than the bottom of the tub."
  },
  {
    "block_id": "b000035",
    "issues": [],
    "kind": "prose",
    "repairs": [
      {
        "left": "p0003-n0012-l0000",
        "operation": "line_wrap_to_space",
        "right": "p0003-n0012-l0001"
      },
      {
        "left": "p0003-n0012-l0001",
        "operation": "line_wrap_to_space",
        "right": "p0003-n0012-l0002"
      }
    ],
    "section_id": "s0005",
    "source_line_ids": [
      "p0003-n0012-l0000",
      "p0003-n0012-l0001",
      "p0003-n0012-l0002"
    ],
    "source_pages": [
      3
    ],
    "text": "To make the temperature consistent, the easiest solution is to cup your hands and circulate the hot water from the side with the faucet to the other side of the tub, and also circulate the hot water from the water surface to the bottom of the top."
  },
  {
    "block_id": "b000036",
    "issues": [],
    "kind": "prose",
    "repairs": [
      {
        "left": "p0003-n0013-l0000",
        "operation": "line_wrap_to_space",
        "right": "p0003-n0013-l0001"
      }
    ],
    "section_id": "s0005",
    "source_line_ids": [
      "p0003-n0013-l0000",
      "p0003-n0013-l0001"
    ],
    "source_pages": [
      3
    ],
    "text": "Another option, however, for those of us who don\u2019t want to spend the duration of our bath \ufb02ailing our arms, is to use our invention, \u201dHome Jacuzzi.\u201d Our invention spans the length and"
  },
  {
